  "title": "# Fable foundation for Molly as one app (xlayout s1-s2 + dock-engine s1-s4) Brett Nov 3 2026 05:44 …",
  "asked": "# Fable foundation for Molly as one app (xlayout s1-s2 + dock-engine s1-s4) Brett Nov 3 2026 05:44 ET: \"Build the molly app that starts with fable.\" This headless run does ONLY the Fable phases below, then stops (the Opus phases follow in another run). xlayout s3 (pane engine) is replaced by the Urgent build dock-engine: build dock-engine s1-s4 instead of xlayout s3, then tick xlayout s3 with note 'covered by dock-engine'. Order: dock-engine s1-s4 first (shared by MD Studio, xLayout, Theme Editor), then xlayout s1, s2. Molly-only for chrome merging: standalone apps stay exactly as they are; Patches is paused, don't touch it. Android on hold: Kotlin twins are deferred gaps in framework/spec/PORTING.md. Tick each step as you go: AXF_BUILD_PROFILE=urgent node apps/console-web/plugins/build-orchestrator/orchestrator.mjs act step dock-engine <sN> done; AXF_BUILD_PROFILE=big-dog node apps/console-web/plugins/build-orchestrator/orchestrator.mjs act step xlayout <sN> done. Update _claude/THREADS.md rows (dock-engine, xLayout) at each step. Commit + push branch claude/molly-fable often; open the PR at the end (push banner merges it). UI Review: DockHost changes are visible, submit desktop + phone shots headlessly with --group \"molly-fable - <Mon D h:mm AM/PM>\". ## Phase A: dock-engine (profile urgent), model Fable Steps (~1.8 h): [ ] s1 (~30m) Engine: split tree (horizontal/vertical), drop zones (any tab header, split edges, centre), undock to floating, re-dock, pane limit, serialize/restore. Extend framework/core/engines/windows (panes, tab groups). [ ] s2 (~25m) Fixture + engine tests; PORTING.md deferred Kotlin twin [ ] s3 (~30m) React DockHost on framework/react/windows/WindowHost: drag tabs between headers, hover drop-zone overlay shows the split, splitter resize, tokens only [ ] s4 (~25m) 10 layout presets as data + preview thumbnails (for xLayout IDE mode and MD Studio IDE view) ## Phase B: xlayout (profile big-dog), model Fable, s1 and s2 only [ ] s1 (~30m) xlayout@1 asset type: chrome-merge model, pane tree (from dock-engine), pane limit, 10 layout presets as data (reuse dock-engine presets), 3 toolbar slots (visible, location), toolbar items + open target (main|floating|pane); asset-types.json, validators, reference engine, fixture [ ] s2 (~30m) Unified chrome engine: merge each app's (AmberX, axHub web, Dev Console) app menu, nav, context menu, toolbars and banner widgets into one namespaced model; guests send chrome as data, host runs picks back (embed@1 takes, Molly host only). Toolbar designer is its OWN plugin (toolbar-designer), reached through a capability service, not built here. [x] s3 covered by dock-engine: tick it with that note. Rules: one session, no sub-agents; Opus or Fable only; steps <= 30 min. Look: every colour, size, spacing, font, radius and border from asset tokens (--fx-*), framework controls, no var() fallbacks; node framework/cli/check-theme.mjs and check-controls.mjs must pass. Change a reference engine -> regenerate framework/spec/fixtures (npx -y tsx framework/spec/gen-fixtures.mts). Stop after Phase B; write the To carry on block in THREADS.md for the Opus phase (xlayout s4-s12). Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, patches-web, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once.",
